<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Turkmenistan</h1><p class="st-meta">1991 CE – present · capital Ashgabat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A gas-rich desert state on the Caspian, one of the world's most closed countries, shaped by the personality cult of Saparmurat Niyazov.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turkmen-ssr">Turkmen SSR</a> declared independence on 27 October 1991 under its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Communist Party</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saparmurat-niyazov">Saparmurat Niyazov</a>, who became president of the new state and in 1999 was made president for life.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saparmurat-niyazov">Niyazov</a> styled himself Turkmenbashi, 'leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a>', and created an elaborate personality cult, with golden statues and his book <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhnama">Ruhnama</a> required reading. He renamed months after himself and his mother. The country declared permanent neutrality, recognised by the UN in 1995. Its economy rests on enormous natural gas reserves, exported mainly to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, while political opposition and independent media are banned.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saparmurat-niyazov">Niyazov</a>'s death in 2006 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurbanguly-berdimuhamedow">Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedow</a> became president, building his own cult. In 2022 his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serdar-berdimuhamedow">Serdar Berdimuhamedow</a> succeeded him, while Gurbanguly kept great influence as chairman of the people's council.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/turkmenistan.jpg" alt="Turkmenistan" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Turkmenistan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1991 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ashgabat</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Saparmurat Niyazov, Gurbanguly Berdimuhamedow, Serdar Berdimuhamedow</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkmen</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkmenistan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Turkmenistan</dd></dl></aside></div>
